learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-03T21:50:55.682Z","harness:codex","Canonical mutation previews must come from the exact locked serialized bytes and shared inline normalizer. File-backed schema hydration belongs to a separate read boundary. Validate after serialization as well as before it: mutable/getter-backed proposals can change between the two. Replay receipts cannot reconstruct an old proposal from current settings."
  "2026-10-03T22:43:46.038Z","harness:codex","Forward compatibility belongs to the source-aware persistence boundary. Canonical projections deliberately omit future fields, so serializing only the projection can lose data even when preview equality is correct. Reuse the normal recursive source-delta serializer and test root plus nested unrecognized fields, dry-run inertness and audited apply history in one real-filesystem contract."
